[ PENHT: READ THE PEN-HIT TABLE (DSPLY P. 30).  WHEN THE LIGHT PEN SEES A
[ LINE WHILE THE PE BIT IS SET, DSPLY ENTERS THE ITEM THAT DREW IT, AND THE
[ IMAGE IT WAS DRAWN IN, IN A CIRCULAR TABLE OF 16 ENTRIES.
[ CALL:  JPSR PENHT; N; ITA; IMA
[ N, ITA AND IMA ARE ADDRESSES: N HOLDS WHICH ENTRY (0 THE LATEST, 1 THE
[ ONE BEFORE ...); THE ITEM'S ADDRESS GOES TO ITA, THE IMAGE'S TO IMA.
[ THE TABLE'S LAYOUT IS OURS: PHT HOLDS THE NUMBER OF HITS SO FAR, THEN
[ TWO WORDS AN ENTRY.  A PROGRAM WAITING FOR A HIT WATCHES PHT CHANGE.
PENHT:  0                       [ THE RETURN ADDRESS GOES HERE
        MDAR'I'X PENHT          [ THE ADDRESS OF N; STEP PAST IT
        ARMD PH.A
        MDAR'I PH.A
        ARMD PH.N               [ N
        MDAR PHT                [ HITS SO FAR
        MDAS'F 17
        MDAS'N PH.N             [ + 15 - N
        MDAR'A PH.M             [ MODULO 16: THE ENTRY
        ARMD PH.T
        MDAS PH.T               [ TWO WORDS AN ENTRY
        MDAS'F PHT+1
        ARMD PH.P
        MDAR'I'X PH.P
        ARMD PH.I               [ THE ITEM
        MDAR'I PH.P
        ARMD PH.J               [ THE IMAGE
        MDAR'I'X PENHT
        ARMD PH.A
        MDAR PH.I
        ARMD'I PH.A             [ TO ITA
        MDAR'I'X PENHT
        ARMD PH.A
        MDAR PH.J
        ARMD'I PH.A             [ TO IMA
        JUMP'I PENHT
PH.A:   0
PH.N:   0
PH.T:   0
PH.P:   0
PH.I:   0
PH.J:   0
PH.M:   17
